================================================================================
libvips, via the @img/sharp-libvips-* prebuilt binaries
================================================================================

The web build depends on `sharp`, which is Apache-2.0, and `sharp` depends on
prebuilt libvips binaries published as `@img/sharp-libvips-*`. Those binaries are
licensed LGPL-3.0-or-later. Four further platform packages —
`@img/sharp-wasm32`, `@img/sharp-win32-arm64`, `@img/sharp-win32-ia32` and
`@img/sharp-win32-x64` — are published under combined terms that include
LGPL-3.0-or-later.

Fourteen such packages are pinned in `apps/web/package-lock.json`. A second
lockfile carried the same fourteen until D-637 deleted the brand tooling and the
workspace that held it. They are:

  @img/sharp-libvips-darwin-arm64      1.3.2    LGPL-3.0-or-later
  @img/sharp-libvips-darwin-x64        1.3.2    LGPL-3.0-or-later
  @img/sharp-libvips-linux-arm         1.3.2    LGPL-3.0-or-later
  @img/sharp-libvips-linux-arm64       1.3.2    LGPL-3.0-or-later
  @img/sharp-libvips-linux-ppc64       1.3.2    LGPL-3.0-or-later
  @img/sharp-libvips-linux-riscv64     1.3.2    LGPL-3.0-or-later
  @img/sharp-libvips-linux-s390x       1.3.2    LGPL-3.0-or-later
  @img/sharp-libvips-linux-x64         1.3.2    LGPL-3.0-or-later
  @img/sharp-libvips-linuxmusl-arm64   1.3.2    LGPL-3.0-or-later
  @img/sharp-libvips-linuxmusl-x64     1.3.2    LGPL-3.0-or-later
  @img/sharp-wasm32                    0.35.3   Apache-2.0 AND LGPL-3.0-or-later AND MIT
  @img/sharp-win32-arm64               0.35.3   Apache-2.0 AND LGPL-3.0-or-later
  @img/sharp-win32-ia32                0.35.3   Apache-2.0 AND LGPL-3.0-or-later
  @img/sharp-win32-x64                 0.35.3   Apache-2.0 AND LGPL-3.0-or-later

libvips is copyright its authors. Its source is at https://github.com/libvips/libvips
and the packaging source for these binaries is at https://github.com/lovell/sharp-libvips.
The full LGPL-3.0 text is at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0.txt and the GPL-3.0
text it incorporates by reference is at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.txt.

These binaries are used unmodified. This repository does not vendor, redistribute
or link them: they are resolved from the npm registry at install time, and only the
lockfile entries pinning them are committed here.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
What this notice does and does not settle
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

It settles the attribution: the dependency is disclosed, its licence is named, and
its source is located. That was the first item of
docs/operations/OPEN_SOURCE_RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md and it was open because nothing in
the repository named these packages at all.

It does not settle the distribution question, and does not pretend to. LGPL-3.0
obligations around a Combined Work — relinking, corresponding source, and the
written offer — attach when a work incorporating the library is conveyed. No such
artifact is built or distributed today: there is no release, no signed binary, and
no TUF root, which item 7 of the checklist records deliberately. When a release set
is first produced, whether it embeds these binaries and what that obliges is a
question for that release, not a question this file answers in advance.

No counsel review has taken place. LICENSES.md says so, D-571 records that legal
paperwork is deprioritised with the exposure knowingly accepted, and neither this
file nor the checklist changes that. An attribution written by an engineer is an
attribution, not a legal opinion.
